meta {
  name: Google Login
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "credential": "paste-a-real-google-id-token-here"
  }
}

docs {
  Authenticates with a Google ID token obtained client-side via Google
  Identity Services (see client/src/components/GoogleSignInButton.jsx).
  The server verifies the token's signature and audience with
  google-auth-library, then finds an existing user by google_id, links an
  existing password account with the same email, or creates a new student
  account - returning the same response shape as Login either way.

  This request can't be exercised directly from Bruno with a fake value:
  Google's servers reject any credential that isn't a real, freshly-issued
  ID token from an actual browser sign-in. Included here for documentation
  completeness - the real flow is demonstrated through the app's UI.
}
